claim.claim-text:
receiving audio data frames, the audio data frames included in audio data packets received at actual packet arrival times during a time interval that corresponds with a conversation analysis segment (205);
analyzing the audio data of the conversation analysis segment to determine network jitter dynamics data and conversational interactivity data, wherein the network jitter dynamics data provides an indication of jitter in a network that relays the audio data packets, wherein the conversational interactivity data provides an indication of interactivity between participants of a conversation represented by the audio data frame (210), and wherein determining the conversational interactivity data involves analyzing the conversational activity of only a single conversational participant;
selecting, based on the network jitter dynamics and the conversational interactivity data (215) of the audio data, a jitter buffer control mode from at least three jitter buffer control modes, wherein each jitter buffer control mode corresponds to a range of jitter buffer sizes; and
determining a jitter buffer size based on the selected jitter buffer control mode.
